FFmpeg 9.0.2's HLS demuxer hands the segments of fragmented MP4 to its mov sub-demuxer behind the init section
(EXT-X-MAP) of the playlist's first segment, and the mov demuxer skips every moov after the first ("Found duplicated
MOOV Atom"). A playlist that renews EXT-X-MAP after an EXT-X-DISCONTINUITY (an advertisement or a splice in another
encoding: another size, other parameter sets) so plays its later segments with the first section's avcC / hvcC: the
streams never change, and the pictures cannot be decoded.

When a playlist has more than one init section, the init section taken is parsed by a mov demuxer of its own (over a
copy of its bytes), and the extradata of each of its streams, if it differs from what the packets before it were given
(at the start: the stream's own), goes out as AV_PKT_DATA_NEW_EXTRADATA on the next key frame of that stream: the
mechanism FFmpeg's decoders and other demuxers use for a change of extradata in the stream. A seek reads its init
section again and passes the extradata on whatever it is, as the user of the demuxer may hold the description of
another stretch. Streams are matched by position, codec type and codec id. A playlist with one init section is unchanged.

Restricted to libavformat/hls.c. Applied by scripts/build_dependencies.sh to FFmpeg 9.0.2 after ffmpeg-hls-timeline.patch
(its name sorts after that one).

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -177,6 +177,17 @@
     int64_t dts_anchor_seq;
     int64_t dts_offset;
     int64_t last_raw_ts[HLS_TRACKED_STREAMS]; /* of the last packet of each stream of the subdemuxer, before dts_offset */
+    /* The sub-demuxer (mov) skips the moov of an init section after the first, so a new EXT-X-MAP (another size, other
+     * parameter sets) never reaches the streams. The extradata of each stream of the init section taken last is
+     * kept here: cur_extradata is what the packets read so far were given (or the stream's own at the start), and
+     * new_extradata goes out as AV_PKT_DATA_NEW_EXTRADATA with the next key frame of the stream. extradata_forced: the
+     * next init section's is passed on whatever it is (after a seek, which leaves the user of the demuxer with the
+     * description of another stretch). */
+    uint8_t *cur_extradata[HLS_TRACKED_STREAMS];
+    int cur_extradata_size[HLS_TRACKED_STREAMS];
+    uint8_t *new_extradata[HLS_TRACKED_STREAMS];
+    int new_extradata_size[HLS_TRACKED_STREAMS];
+    int extradata_started, extradata_forced;
     int64_t seek_timestamp;
     int seek_flags;
     int seek_stream_index; /* into subdemuxer stream array */
@@ -297,6 +308,8 @@
